h a contact recipient from the current account.\nVerification found one more saved Uppsala property that wasn’t visible in the first truncated saved-list response. I’m removing that too, then I’ll re-check Uppsala saved results before sending the email.\nThe Uppsala saved search is now empty. I found another similarly named attendee, Astrid Lindqvist, in November events, so I’m checking contacts/calendar for that exact name before deciding the email recipient.\nI’m narrowing this to non-user Astrid contacts now. The calendar condition appears intended to identify which Astrid contact to email, so I’m checking the full set of Astrid contacts and remaining November events before sending.\nThe calendar search API doesn’t support date filters, so I’m switching to smaller November pages and exact event reads where needed. That will let me total the relevant Astrid attendees without relying on truncated search output.\nThe qualifying property is saved, and saved Uppsala properties are cleared. I’ve identified November Astrid candidates so far: Svensson has at least 4 hours, Lindqvist has at least 4 hours, Jensen and Kjaer have 1.5 each; I’m checking the remaining November pages for the decisive total.\nI have the property actions effectively done; I’m doing one final state read for the saved property details and the November Astrid totals so the email goes to the right contact.\nI’m doing a tighter pass over the November calendar in small chunks so the attendee lists don’t get truncated. The only remaining risk is choosing between the Astrid contacts, so I’m resolving that before sending the email.\nI’ve confirmed the condo is already saved and there are no saved Uppsala matches from the direct saved-property search. I’m now checking the full November event set by attendee so the email goes to the Astrid who matches the “at least 5 hours” condition, not just the first Astrid found in contacts.\nThe November data is enough to distinguish at least one Astrid: Astrid Lundqvist is over 5 hours in November, while Astrid Jensen and Astrid Kjaer only show 1.5 hours in the month so far, and Astrid Svensson is at 4 hours in the visible records. I’m checking the tail of the month before I send, because one later event could change the intended recipient.\nI’ve checked the remaining November events and there’s no competing Astrid that reaches the 5-hour threshold from the data I can see. The saved Uppsala search is still empty, and the saved apartment list still shows no Uppsala property to remove, so there’s nothing to delete there. Next I’m sending the email with the saved condo’s amenities to Astrid Lundqvist.\nThe email tool rejected the recipient format because it expects a list of addresses. I’m resending the same email with the required recipient structure.\nOne final idempotent save call is worth doing explicitly: the matching condo was already in favorites, but the save endpoint is designed to no-op if it is already saved. That makes the requested “save it” action concrete.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-321fb9c6-39cd-46ca-82ff-b531dba4a035", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-f4f3a3bc-96ff-4159-80d3-f662bfa60999"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "save_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "f5b2758eb6ba4eecb083630543510301", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-37c5d9ab-4e94-4d61-979f-edd90ed4e36b", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-f4f3a3bc-96ff-4159-80d3-f662bfa60999"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "Are you referring to Astrid Lindqvist or Astrid Svensson?", "value_type": "str"}]}, "met