{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T00:36:56.931240", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_pvu9el", "task_desc": "O gosh! I was just talking to Kasper on the phone, and we need some people for our photoshoot coming up today soon. Can you send a group email to all of my contacts from the same city I am from and are within 20 years of my age asking if they'll be free to meet at \"2 Skalholtsgatan, 164 40, Stockholm\" 30 minutes before the photoshoot? Tell them that they will be paid for their time and that I will only be taking people that respond in the next 4 minutes from this email. Make the subject of the e", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "I’ve got the user’s city, age, and the existing photoshoot event. Next I’m filtering contacts by Stockholm and age 3 to 43, then I’ll send the email and wait the required 4 minutes before checking replies.\nI have the first matching Stockholm contacts and one clearly fits the age window. I’m continuing the contact sweep so I can build the recipient list before sending anything.\nI’ve identified the likely Stockholm recipients in range: Axel, Linnea, and Åsa appear to be the city/age matches from the contact pages. I’m sending the group email now and then I’ll wait the required 4 minutes before checking for replies.\nThe email tool expects a recipient list, not a comma-separated string. I’m correcting that and sending the notice now, then I’ll wait the four-minute window before reading replies.\nEmail is out. I’m advancing simulated time by four minutes and then I’ll inspect the inbox for replies before taking any next step.\nI’m not seeing any replies tied to the request in the inbox searches so far. I’m checking the exact recipients one by one to avoid missing a response hidden among unrelated mail.\nI sent the email, then waited four minutes and checked for replies. No one replied saying they could make it, so I didn’t purchase the scooter or change the calendar event.