y near the cutoff at 36 that must be excluded. I’m finishing the roster sweep now and then I’ll create the group with only the qualifying contacts.\nI have the last pages. I’m identifying the Stockholm contacts at or below 35 now; the remainder are clearly out of scope, so I can move to the actual group creation once I confirm the full participant list.\nI’ve got enough of the later pages to see the remaining Stockholm candidates. I’m now checking for the final Stockholm entries and then I’ll create the group with everyone who actually fits.\nI’ve reached the Stockholm cluster. I’m checking the tail of the list for any last qualifying contacts and for the coach entry; once that’s settled I can create the group and start the reply watch.\nThere’s one more Stockholm contact at the age boundary. I’m confirming the last slice so I don’t miss anyone under 35 and then I’ll move to the message and monitoring phase.\nI have the likely Stockholm matches, but I still need the exact coach contact to exclude it cleanly. I’m doing a direct search for Stockholm and coach-related entries so the group membership is correct before I send anything.\nI’ve ruled out the contact search shortcut. I’m finishing the roster scan directly from the contacts list so I can separate the real Stockholm matches from the rest and avoid guessing at the girlfriend exclusion.\nI have the core Stockholm set. I’m doing one last pass through the remaining entries to confirm there isn’t another Stockholm contact under 35 and to verify the coach exclusion before I create the group.\nI’ve confirmed the remaining pages. The contacts that fit are the Stockholm entries under 35, and the 35-year-old Stockholm contact is excluded by the age cutoff; I’m now creating the group conversation with the qualifying people and sending the note.\nI found the actual Stockholm under-35 pair and the earlier attempts were off because one phone was guessed wrong and one contact was over the age limit. I’m checking whether the 